  "result": "This isn't really a \"ship blind\" situation \u2014 double-charging customers is a financial/compliance issue, not just a UX bug, so the risk-acceptance needs to be explicit and documented (not just \"everyone already knows\"), ideally with sign-off from whoever owns payments risk/compliance, plus a note in the release/incident log with the known rate and duration.\n\nThe bigger question is whether there's a fast stopgap short of the full fix \u2014 retry double-charge bugs are often mitigated cheaply with an idempotency key on the charge request (so a retried call safely no-ops if the original succeeded) even if the underlying race condition isn't fully fixed. That's usually a much smaller change than the full retry-logic fix.\n\nWant me to look at the actual retry code to see if an idempotency-key stopgap is feasible before today's cutoff, or are you just looking for how to frame the risk-acceptance/communication?",
